#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:1
msgid "概念：硬件投影与约束证据"
msgstr "Concept: Hardware projection and constraint evidence"

#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:3
msgid "每个 step，动作是归一化的电流增量，硬件模型把它映射进合法区间。合法增量由三个边界联合定义："
msgstr "At each step the action is a normalized current delta that the hardware model maps into the legal interval. The legal increment is defined jointly by three bounds:"

#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:5
msgid "电流边界：新电流必须在 `[current_lower_a, current_upper_a]`。"
msgstr "Current bounds: the new current must lie in `[current_lower_a, current_upper_a]`."

#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:6
msgid "爬升率边界：每步增量不能超过 `slew_rate_upper_a_per_s * timestep_seconds`。"
msgstr "Slew-rate bound: the per-step increment cannot exceed `slew_rate_upper_a_per_s * timestep_seconds`."

#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:7
msgid "电压推导边界：由电阻、电压上限和电流变化联合推导。"
msgstr "Voltage-derived bound: derived jointly from resistance, the voltage limit, and the current change."

#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:9
msgid "非法动作有两种显式行为，由构建时声明的 `constraint_mode` 决定："
msgstr "Illegal actions have two explicit behaviors, chosen at build time by `constraint_mode`:"

#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:11
msgid "`project_and_report`：把动作投影进合法区间，在 `info` 里同时给出请求动作、实际动作和约束证据。"
msgstr "`project_and_report`: the action is projected into the legal interval and `info` reports the requested action, the applied action, and constraint evidence."

#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:12
msgid "`terminate`：非法动作直接终止本回合。"
msgstr "`terminate`: an illegal action ends the episode immediately."

#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:14
msgid "**不存在静默裁剪**：要么给出证据，要么结束回合。下游代码可以通过 `info` 看到当前生效的约束，而不是事后猜测。"
msgstr "**There is no silent clipping**: either evidence is provided or the episode ends. Downstream code sees the effective constraints in `info` instead of guessing after the fact."

#: ../../concepts/hardware-projection.md:16
msgid "硬件字段的声明方式见[操作指南：硬件与场景](../how-to/hardware-scenarios)。"
msgstr "How hardware fields are declared: [How-to: hardware and scenarios](../how-to/hardware-scenarios)."
